=== ARM P (paired) pre-registration (stamped 2026-09-13 08:16 UTC, before launch) — does the #434 fix let lever N break the doom loop? PINNED basin, flag-only toggle, on 10-rule-in-pyproject / 35B
Motivation: arm N (plan-autoadvance-10-preregistration.log) FAILED N3 — the advance fired but the one triggered ON run still doom-looped — for two now-fixed bugs (#434): a same-title parent/child carryover collision (advance never stuck) and a doom-guard that counts identical submissions not harness progress (a sticking advance still races the exact-repeat guard). The N3 read rested on n=1 because --no-pin STARVED the ON arm of triggers (ON 1/9 vs OFF 4/9, UNPAIRED basins). Arm P removes that confound by PINNING the workspace so OFF and ON get the byte-identical prompt / basin and differ ONLY by the flag.
Build: main at ce882c3 (#434 merged) — the fixed lever-N build (collision fix + doom-guard reset + lever N), deployed to /opt/zak-code-bench/src (fix a: 2 sites in tasks.py; fix b: last_autoadvanced wired in both loop paths, verified on the box). ONE build; ZAKCODE_PLAN_AUTOADVANCE is the ONLY difference.
Design: PINNED mode (run_task.py ZBENCH_PIN_IDENTITY -> constant workspace /tmp/zbench-pinned-10-rule-in-pyproject, wiped and re-seeded each run), so every run gets the byte-identical prompt (35B, temp 0, stable identity, survey ON, verify_auto OFF). Interleave OFF, ON, OFF, ON ... 5 tight pairs (10 runs) to bound endpoint drift WITHIN a pair. Under pinned+temp0 the trajectory is reproducible given stable endpoint, so within a pair OFF and ON differ only by the flag on the SAME basin. Runner /root/zb-armp.sh; JSONs bench/results/determinism-zakcode-pin1-temp0-10-rule-in-pyproject.P-{OFF,ON}-35B-10-p{1..5}.json; dumps /root/zb-dumps/P-* (never committed).
Instruments per run: verify_rc (pass=0), stop_reason, num_turns, trace_interventions[plan_autoadvance] (adv) and [plan_unchanged]; from the largest wire dump (rb-10853) the identical-submission streak (the trigger) and the FINAL plan-completion state (is the plan N/N done?).
Rules (applied by the letter):
  P1 (trigger present, pinned): >= 1 OFF run enters the resend pattern (doom_loop, or plan_unchanged/advance receipts in its dump). If 0 OFF runs trigger, the pinned basin is not a doom-basin under the current endpoint state -> re-pin to a fresh fixed workspace and retry up to 2 re-pins; if still 0, arm P is INCONCLUSIVE in situ and the deterministic loop repro (#434 tests) stands as the primary evidence. N1's lesson: the trigger is measured first.
  P2 (wiring, re-confirm): every triggered ON run fires the advance (adv >= 1 in the dump AND trace_interventions.plan_autoadvance >= 1). Already confirmed in arm N in situ; re-confirm on the pinned basin.
  P3 (PRIMARY — the fix lets the harness walk the loop to completion): among pairs whose OFF member doom-loops with an INCOMPLETE plan and verify_rc=1, the paired ON member (same basin) reaches a COMPLETE plan (final plan N/N in the dump) AND passes verify (verify_rc=0). STRONG win = ON stop_reason=completed; PARTIAL win = ON stop_reason=doom_loop but plan complete + verify=0 (the harness walked it, the model kept resending after — the loop-repro shape); FAIL = ON doom-loops with an incomplete plan (the fix did not help). Prediction: every triggered pair is a STRONG or PARTIAL win, never a FAIL; verify_rc is ground truth against a false-completion.
  P4 (no regression on a healthy pinned basin): if the pinned basin does NOT trigger, OFF and ON both complete and pass at comparable turns (the flag is inert with no resend) — the arm N N5/N6 controls, re-confirmed paired.
Threats: endpoint drift across the ~35-min run can shift the basin between pairs (arm M saw a modal shift ~15:00); tight OFF/ON interleaving bounds within-pair drift, and P1's re-pin covers a non-triggering basin. A pinned doom-basin reproduces ONE trajectory across OFF runs (distinct-trajectory N = 1), but P3 is exactly "does the fix change that one trajectory's outcome" — the clean test the unpaired arm could not run. A false ON completion (plan marked done, work absent) is caught by verify_rc (P3).
